@startuml
autonumber
skinparam Style strictuml
skinparam MaxMessageSize 250
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20

title MatchToCollab - Sequence Diagram (caa 6 April 2026)

actor "User A" as UA
actor "User B" as UB
participant "Nginx" as NX
box "API Gateway (Auth + Orchestrator)" #LightYellow
    participant "Gateway" as GW
end box
box "Matching Service" #LightBlue
    participant "Match Router" as MS
    participant "Match Worker" as MW
end box
participant "Question Service" as QS
participant "Collab Service" as Collab
database "Redis\n(Matching DB)" as RM
database "Redis\n(Sessions DB)" as RS

== Phase 1: Matching (Polling-based) ==

UA -> NX: POST /api/matching/find-pair (JWT_A, criteria)
NX -> GW: Forward (strip /api)
GW -> GW: Verify JWT_A (uid_A)
GW -> MS: POST /matching/find-pair (X-User-Id: uid_A)
MS -> RM: LPUSH incoming_match_queue {uid_A, ticket_id_A, ...}
MS --> GW: 202 Accepted {ticket_id_A, poll_url}
GW --> UA: 202 Accepted {ticket_id_A, poll_url}

note over UA, MS: User A attempts to poll for status, but match not found yet

UA -> NX: GET /api/matching/find-pair/status/{ticket_id_A}
NX -> GW: Forward
GW -> MS: GET /matching/find-pair/status/{ticket_id_A}
MS -> RM: GET match_result:{ticket_id_A}
RM --> MS: null
MS --> GW: 202 Accepted (pending)
GW --> UA: 202 Accepted (pending)

note over UA, MS: User B joins the queue some time later...

UB -> NX: POST /api/matching/find-pair (JWT_B, criteria)
NX -> GW: Forward
GW -> MS: POST /matching/find-pair (X-User-Id: uid_B)
MS -> RM: LPUSH incoming_match_queue {uid_B, ticket_id_B, ...}
MS --> GW: 202 Accepted {ticket_id_B}
GW --> UB: 202 Accepted {ticket_id_B}

MW -> RM: BRPOP incoming_match_queue
RM --> MW: {uid_B, ...}
MW -> MW: Match Found (UA & UB)
MW -> RM: SETEX match_result:{ticket_id_A} {status: success, peer_id: uid_B, ...}
MW -> RM: SETEX match_result:{ticket_id_B} {status: success, peer_id: uid_A, ...}

UA -> NX: GET /api/matching/find-pair/status/{ticket_id_A}
NX -> GW: Forward
GW -> MS: GET /matching/find-pair/status/{ticket_id_A}
MS -> RM: GET match_result:{ticket_id_A}
RM --> MS: {status: success, peer_id: uid_B, ...}
MS --> GW: 200 OK {match_data}
GW --> UA: 200 OK {match_data}

UB -> NX: GET /api/matching/find-pair/status/{ticket_id_B}
NX -> GW: Forward
GW -> MS: GET /matching/find-pair/status/{ticket_id_B}
MS -> RM: GET match_result:{ticket_id_B}
RM --> MS: {status: success, peer_id: uid_A, ...}
MS --> GW: 200 OK {match_data}
GW --> UB: 200 OK {match_data}

== Phase 2: Distributed Session Initialization (API Gateway) ==

note over UA, GW
  Both matched users simultaneously hit the Gateway's /session/init endpoint.
  The Gateway uses a Redis lock to elect a Leader to provision the room. (Avoids race conditions)
end note

UA -> NX: POST /api/session/init {peer_id: uid_B, topic, difficulty}
NX -> GW: Forward
UB -> NX: POST /api/session/init {peer_id: uid_A, topic, difficulty}
NX -> GW: Forward

GW -> GW: Generate lock_key = lock:match:{user_min}:{user_max}
GW -> GW: Generate room_id = UUID

GW -> RS: SETNX lock_key room_id
RS --> GW: 1 (Leader) or 0 (Follower)

group Leader Logic (e.g., UA's request)
    GW -> QS: GET /question?topic=X&difficulty=Y
    QS --> GW: {question_id: "q_101", ...}
    GW -> RS: SET session:{room_id}:meta {users, questionId, topic, diff, startedAt}
    GW -> RS: SET active_session:{uid_A} room_id
    GW -> RS: SET active_session:{uid_B} room_id
    GW --> UA: 200 OK {room_id}
end

group Follower Logic (e.g., UB's request)
    GW -> RS: GET lock_key
    RS --> GW: room_id
    GW -> RS: POLL session:{room_id}:meta (until exists)
    RS --> GW: {meta}
    GW --> UB: 200 OK {room_id}
end

== Phase 3: Ticket Acquisition & WebSocket Connection ==

note over UA, GW
  Users transition to the Collaboration Page.
  See **docs/plantUML/collab.puml** for detailed Ticket and WS flow.
end note

UA -> NX: POST /api/collab/join {room_id}
NX -> GW: Forward
GW -> Collab: POST /collab/join (X-User-Id: uid_A, room_id)
Collab --> GW: {ticket: "UUID_1"}
GW --> UA: {ticket: "UUID_1"}

UA -> NX: WS /socket.io/?ticket=UUID_1
NX -> Collab: Proxy Upgrade

== Phase 4: Real-time Collaboration ==

group /editor namespace (Yjs Sync)
    UA -> Collab: yjs-update (binary delta)
    Collab -> UB: Broadcast yjs-update
end

group /chat namespace
    UA -> Collab: send-message ({text})
    Collab -> UB: Broadcast receive-message
end

note over Collab
  Collaboration uses Yjs for editor sync and Socket.io for chat.
  State is persisted in Redis Sessions DB.
end note
@enduml
